To find the next numbers in this sequence where each term increases by a constant amount (which is common difference), we can simply add that same increment to the last given number. Here, it appears Umi adds 20 every time:  
80 + 20 = 100 for the fifth number;   
100 + 20 = 120 for the sixth number; and so on... until we reach our eighth term which is A) 160.
